# [BPM](../wg/bpm.html)

## Summary

The BPM Working Group held its second session at IETF 127 in San Francisco on Wednesday. The session focused on proposed new work, benchmarking methodologies, on-path telemetry extensions, and brief lightning presentations. The chairs emphasized the working group's policy to prioritize draft progression and meeting agenda time for documents with running code, hackathon implementations, or interop experience. Key technical topics included OAM/IOAM extensions for on-path delay, the IOAM Global Opaque Block (GOB), benchmarking methodologies for AI agents and RPKI/ROV, framework guidance for interpreting measurement results, and several short lightning presentations.

